      "text": "@omarsar0 an Opus-evolved harness starting at 68.41 on Gemini, below the 73.89 plain seed, says it plainly: edits that help one model can quietly hurt another. my guess is SIM works partly because predicted vs observed outcome exposes which edits were model-specific. does the memory record",
